WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:05.520
When a person is smoking cannabis, one&nbsp;
of the plant’s chemicals known as THC,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:05.520 --> 00:00:12.480
passes from the lungs into the bloodstream. The&nbsp;
THC is then carried by the blood to the brain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.480 --> 00:00:16.140
where it acts on specific cannabinoid receptors.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:23.460
These receptors are found in areas of&nbsp;
the brain associated with: concentration,&nbsp;

00:00:23.460 --> 00:00:26.100
thinking,
time perception,&nbsp;

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:28.560
coordination,
memory,&nbsp;

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:30.420
and sensory pleasures.

00:00:31.860 --> 00:00:38.400
The effects of THC activation in these areas&nbsp;
is responsible for the “high” that people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:43.740
feel. But besides creating an altered&nbsp;
state of mind, something else happens.

00:00:48.300 --> 00:00:57.600
In the United States, according to a 2018 survey,&nbsp;
1 in 8 adolescents aged 12 to 17, consumed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.600 --> 00:01:05.520
marijuana in the past year. In 12th grade, about&nbsp;
1 in 16 do so daily. So - what’s the problem?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:12.660
Even super smart people smoke, right? Let’s look&nbsp;
at the effect of cannabis on a teenager's brain!

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:20.040
The brain's response to counter the&nbsp;
effects of THC impairs it’s attention,&nbsp;

00:01:20.040 --> 00:01:24.600
its ability to remember, and&nbsp;
its potential for learning.

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:29.100
These Effects can last up to&nbsp;
several days. This would not be&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:33.720
such a problem if our brain ran like&nbsp;
a machine. But that’s not the case.

00:01:35.880 --> 00:01:41.820
The brain is a living organism — maybe the&nbsp;
most precious one there is. In teeangers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.820 --> 00:01:47.340
that organism is still immature. It&nbsp;
takes about 25 years for the human&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:52.440
brain to be fully developed. This is&nbsp;
why when teenagers and adults argue,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:57.780
they often come to different conclusions.&nbsp;
There is a biological reason for that.

00:01:59.820 --> 00:02:03.480
Adults have a fully developed prefrontal cortex,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:08.520
the part of the brain that is responsible&nbsp;
for judgment and an awareness of long-term&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.520 --> 00:02:14.520
consequences. The cortex of teenagers is&nbsp;
still growing. They are more influenced&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.520 --> 00:02:19.620
by their already matured limbic system,&nbsp;
which responds to fears and emotions.

00:02:21.960 --> 00:02:25.980
If the developing brain is&nbsp;
exposed to a lot of THC,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.980 --> 00:02:32.580
the part responsible for controlling emotions&nbsp;
may never reach its full potential. This can&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.580 --> 00:02:38.820
have long-term consequences and effects on one's&nbsp;
measurable intelligence, learning and judgment.

00:02:40.980 --> 00:02:46.560
One study that followed 13 year olds&nbsp;
for 25 years has found that those who&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:52.500
regularly consume marijuana lose on&nbsp;
average 5.8 IQ points by the time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.500 --> 00:02:58.740
they reach adulthood. Since our average&nbsp;
IQ is just 100, that is enough to shut&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:58.740 --> 00:03:03.600
the door to a good college or close the&nbsp;
opportunity to work at a great company.

00:03:03.600 --> 00:03:05.340
But that’s not all.

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:11.700
There is also evidence that some&nbsp;
teenagers that use cannabis are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.700 --> 00:03:17.760
at higher risk of developing depression&nbsp;
or even a psychosis. A psychosis changes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:17.760 --> 00:03:22.800
the way the brain processes information,&nbsp;
and causes you to lose touch with reality.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.800 --> 00:03:28.380
You can see and hear things that aren't&nbsp;
real and may completely lose your mind.

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:36.780
In short, the high of cannabis comes with a&nbsp;
multitude of side-effects. Some might be fun,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:43.020
some might be healing, and some are&nbsp;
potentially horrible — we don’t always know.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:49.680
If you want to live life with the ultimate&nbsp;
learning machine inside your head,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.680 --> 00:03:54.840
you might want to wait until your mind&nbsp;
is fully developed before trying weed.

00:03:56.880 --> 00:04:02.520
What are your thoughts? Did you ever try&nbsp;
cannabis as a teenager? And if so, do you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:02.520 --> 00:04:08.400
think it did damage to your mind or not? Please&nbsp;
share your experiences in the comments below!

